w: 1.~To thee, O God, do _ we give thanks, we do give _ thanks to thee; _ Be- cause thy won- drous works de- clare thy great _ name _ near to be.
w: 2.~I pur- pose, when I _ shall re- ceive the con- gre- _ ga- ti- on, _ That I shall judg- ment u- prigh- tly ren- der _ to _ ev’- ry one.
w: * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
w: 4.~I to the fool- ish _ peo- ple said, Do not deal _ foo- lish- ly; _ And un- to those that wi- cked are, Lift not _ your _ horn on high.
w: 5.~Lift not your horn on _ high, nor speak with stub- born _ neck. But know, _ That not from east, nor west, nor south, pro- mo- _ ti- _ on doth flow.
w: 6.~But God is judge; he _ puts down one, and sets a- _ no- ther up. _ For in the hand of God most high of red _ wine _ is a cup:
w: 7.~‘Tis full of mix- ture, _ he pours forth, and makes the _ wi- cked all _ Wring out the bit- ter dregs there- of; yea, and _ they _ drink them shall.
w: 8.~But I for ev- er _ will de- clare, I Ja- cob’s _ God will praise. _ All horns of lewd men I’ll cut off; but just _ men’s _ horns will raise.
